WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.330
After the birth of Jane Ives, the telekinetically
powered girl commonly known as Eleven, in

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:08.330
1971, Dr. Martin Brenner could only perform
limited experiments until she was old enough

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:12.290
to perform some larger tests. These tests
are what led her to interacting with the Demogorgon

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.760
in roughly 1983, but it’s history may go
much deeper than what we see on screen.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.990
The Demogorgon is an other-worldly creature,
so to understand it we’re going to look

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.690
at how it’s form was inspired by the beasts
of our world, and analyze it’s story seen

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.240
in Stranger Things and the Stranger Things
comic series. I’ll also be exploring what

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.570
really happened to the Demogorgon, and the
hidden connection it shares with Eleven so

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.780
stick around to the end of this video to hear
all about it.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.592
This video is sponsored by Raycon.

00:00:35.592 --> 00:00:40.160
(chaotic piano)

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:43.840
The Demogorgon is a monster from an alternate
dimension that spent its life in darkness

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.090
and decay; stalking around the area referred
to as Mirkwood to find its next meal before

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.450
slipping back behind the curtain that separates
its cold abyss from our own dimension. Welcome

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.710
to Horror History -- in this video I’ll
just be covering the being known as The Demogorgon,

00:00:56.710 --> 00:00:59.860
and in future videos I’ll go over other
members of the Demogorgon species. It’s

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.430
kind of like how in Alien we have the Xenomorph,
who is also part of the Xenomorph species.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:08.249
The actual name of The Demogorgon (or it’s
species) is not known, the characters just

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:11.759
come up with that name based on this Demon
Prince character from the game they’re playing,

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:15.369
Dungeons and Dragons, which may be partially
based off of the forbidden primeval god from

00:01:15.369 --> 00:01:16.759
Ancient Greek mythology.

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:20.779
Not much is known about the Demogorgon prior
to its appearance in Hawkins, however in analyzing

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:24.368
what the Demogorgon truly represents and embodies
to the community of Hawkins, we have to take

00:01:24.368 --> 00:01:29.648
this all the way back to the 1940s. ROLL THE
HORROR HISTORY SCREEN.

00:01:29.648 --> 00:01:32.679
(old timey-piano)

00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:37.530
With the Cold War spanning the majority of
the 20th Century, Americans were generally

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:41.009
concerned about communism spreading through
their communities and the government. This

00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:44.569
eventually led to McCarthyism and Truman’s
Loyalty Program in an attempt to curb the

00:01:44.569 --> 00:01:49.770
worries of the citizens. McCarthyism was a
campaign from 1950-1954 that was run by Senator

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:54.069
Joseph McCarthy, who claimed there were communists
hiding in plain sight in the US Government,

00:01:54.069 --> 00:01:57.239
along with other major institutions. It’s
basically like how there are people who are

00:01:57.239 --> 00:02:00.759
subscribed to this channel, but they don’t
have the deathbell on, like I know you’re

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:02.479
out there. And I WILL FIND YOU.

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.279
McCarthyism devolved into basically an early
version of cancel culture where people who

00:02:06.279 --> 00:02:11.310
maybe weren’t communist ended up on blacklists
and sometimes lost their jobs. So The Truman

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.810
Loyalty Program was made to root out communists
and prevent them from entering government

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.420
positions but you’re probably wondering
what the FRICK this has to do with old flowerface

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.501
over here -- I swear, I’m getting to that.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:25.000
So you may remember in Season 3, semi-spoiler
alert for Season 3 I guess, that the kids discover

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.340
a whole Russian communist operation hidden
underneath the town. But the original Demogorgon

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.290
and the experiments at Hawkins lab served
as a more covert symbol for the communist

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:37.580
agenda way back in the first season. I don’t
know why I’m saying way, back as if it was

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:38.580
that long ago.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.459
So anyway, the US Central Intelligence Agency
was disturbed and intrigued by prisoners of

00:02:42.459 --> 00:02:46.519
war coming back from The Korean War and talking
about communist propaganda, and they believed

00:02:46.519 --> 00:02:51.269
this could be a form of Russian mind control,
so they launched project MK-ULTRA in April

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:55.829
of 1953. Despite how it sounds, this was no
electronic music festival. They used certain

00:02:55.829 --> 00:02:59.799
active substances to try make advancements
in mind control to combat Russia.

00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:04.269
In Stranger Things, the Hawkins National Lab
uses MK Ultra to explain how Eleven might

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:07.609
have obtained her psychokinetic abilities
-- it’s suggested through her mother’s

00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:11.969
participation in secret experiments that continued
on past the initial end of MK-ULTRA, which

00:03:11.969 --> 00:03:16.690
was sometime in 1973. You can actually see
MK-ULTRA included in part of an article title

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:20.719
in a newspaper story about Hawkins Laboratory
that Hopper finds in the library. This article

00:03:20.719 --> 00:03:25.250
is potentially from around 1975, which is
when some details of the project were initially

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.439
released to the public.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:30.249
So the fear of trouble in Hawkins that arises
when residents start going missing, is akin

00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:35.030
the hysteria that swept America during the
communist scare lasting until the USSR dissolved

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.030
in the early 90s.

00:03:36.030 --> 00:03:39.580
It’s been suggested that the Demogorgon
is the Upside-Down version of El, seeing as

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.329
how they are the only ones of their kind so
far to exhibit telekinesis. There are other

00:03:43.329 --> 00:03:45.060
examples, which we’ll get to...

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.209
Eleven was born in ‘71, but Dr. Brenner
held larger tests that led her to interaction

00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:54.029
with the Demogorgon in roughly 1983. Her first
“encounter” with it is when she’s sent

00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:57.450
telepathically to listen to a Russian man’s
conversation. We don’t see the Demogorgon

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:01.959
in this scene however, we are able to hear
its screech, or is it a roar? This could be

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:06.049
because Eleven and the Demogorgon are linked,
and its scream is because it shares the same

00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:09.720
fear that she holds being forced into the
deprivation tank. The scream sounds like a

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.079
cross between a dinosaur and a slowed down
orangutan.

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:16.310
(orangutan calls)

00:04:16.468 --> 00:04:18.414
(Demogorgon cry)

00:04:18.414 --> 00:04:21.750
It also sounds a little bit like me whenever
I get put on hold.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.396
- [Automated Voice] All representatives are currently assisting other customers. Please stay on the line.

00:04:25.396 --> 00:04:26.246
- (ROAR)

00:04:26.246 --> 00:04:30.160
Eleven is encouraged by Brenner to face the
monster she saw again by diving back into

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.020
the sensory deprivation tanks. When she does
find it, the Demogorgon feeds on what looks

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:37.990
like either a giant egg, similar to the one
seen in the Upside-Down, or a tree stump covered

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:38.990
in sap.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.830
Only when she touches its back is when it
finally acknowledges her and lets out a massive…

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:43.830
roar?

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.547
- [Automated voice] We're sorry. All of our representatives are still busy.

00:04:46.547 --> 00:04:47.547
- (ROAR)

00:04:47.547 --> 00:04:51.389
This scares Eleven back into our reality once
she’s met with the Demogorgon’s face,

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:55.020
which opens like a series of flower petals
resembling a squid’s tentacles opening to

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.370
engulf its prey. The Demogorgon has a series
of sharp canines while squids have sharp rings

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.699
on their clubbed tentacles, to help grip their
prey to effectively rip it apart. The comparison

00:05:03.699 --> 00:05:07.280
holds up in later scenes, where we see the
Demogorgon eating in a similar style... including

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.430
the squid’s tendency to start eating prey
while it’s still alive like one of those

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.090
Korean Mukbang chicks.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:15.860
The next time the Demogorgon appears is when
the gate between the Upside-Down and our dimension

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:20.150
is opened on November 6th, 1983. It takes
this chance to hunt everyone in the lab that

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:23.710
it can locate. We can assume it devoured as
much as it could in this short timespan in

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.730
a similar way to how some carnivores engage
in what is known as opportunity hunting, for

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:30.850
example, you’ll see Bears do this, because
they need to quickly gain enough weight for

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:31.850
hibernation.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:35.789
The Demogorgon, could share a similar mentality
since fresh food is usually a limited resource

00:05:35.789 --> 00:05:39.729
for it in the Upside-Down, which is mainly
void of other lifeforms. You’ll also notice

00:05:39.729 --> 00:05:43.419
Eleven also has to relieve her hunger around
this time, but her victims come in the form

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:44.530
of Eggo waffles.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.250
Rather than returning to the Upside-Down,
the flowerface becomes the enemy in the shadows

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:52.410
and begins roaming the woods around town for
fresh prey. It specifically stays in the same

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:56.080
area Will and his friends call ‘Mirkwood’
. The area it stays in is small because it’s

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.960
the closest area to the portal and because
it’s the same area that Will is hiding in

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.150
in the Upside-Down.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:05.030
On the surface, Hawkins is your standard,
small-town America where nothing really happens

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:08.660
and everyone is somewhat familiar with each
other. It’s 1983 and most of the families

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:13.039
we see are the typical ‘Nuclear Family’.
The Cold War frequently comes up in conversation,

00:06:13.039 --> 00:06:16.629
usually through the references of Russian
“commies” or “communists”. While Hawkins

00:06:16.629 --> 00:06:20.450
doesn’t stand out as being special and is
meant to be the stereotypical small town from

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:24.440
the 80s, it does highlight the nagging sense
of anxiety that anyone around you could be

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.060
a communist below the surface.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:30.460
For the residents, life is fairly simple with
lines being drawn to distinguish what is considered

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:34.800
normal and what is not. Things that are “not
normal” are frequently met with criticism

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:38.830
and disbelief, which reflects on the mentality
during the Cold War where Americans were on

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.820
high alert about potential communists.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.470
This is reflected in how the town treats certain
families. The Byers’ live in a secluded

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:48.880
area that’s just outside of town and Joyce
is divorced. Despite having two kids and a

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.490
dog, they don’t fit the standard white picket
fence idea of a perfect family. The series

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:56.879
even opens with a peek into how their lifestyle
is not-so-average. With it, Jonathan has taken

00:06:56.879 --> 00:07:00.530
an almost father-like role, while also trying
to be Will’s older brother.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:04.389
Then we have the Wheeler family. They serve
as what is considered the typical nuclear

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:07.909
family. Nancy describes her parents’ marriage
as her mother marrying well, finding the perfect

00:07:07.909 --> 00:07:12.298
house at the end of a cul-de-sac, and raising
the perfect family in the perfect house.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.895
- I don't think my parents ever loved each other.

00:07:16.293 --> 00:07:18.293
- They must have married for some reason.

00:07:18.294 --> 00:07:19.335
- My Mom was young.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.712
My Dad was older. And he had a cushy job.

00:07:24.478 --> 00:07:27.483
Money. Came from a good family.

00:07:28.856 --> 00:07:31.769
So they bought a nice house at the end of the cul-de-sac.

00:07:32.642 --> 00:07:34.642
And started their nuclear family.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:38.610
- Then she perfectly shoots a can when she’s
never handled a gun before, the same way she

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:40.710
gets everything right on her flashcards.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:44.909
On the night of November 6th, Will Byers is
going home after a D&amp;D campaign with his friends,

00:07:44.909 --> 00:07:48.259
and cuts through Mirkwood. This is when The
Demogorgon comes after Will, and the lights

00:07:48.259 --> 00:07:51.680
flicker as he runs from it. We don’t see
the monster in this scene, but we can hear

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.680
it screeching in the night. This could potentially
be it using sound in a similar way to how

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.500
bats use sonar waves to detect objects in
order to navigate through the dark, since

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.620
the Demogorgon doesn’t appear to have eyes.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.539
Nancy and Jonathan also later determine that
the Demogorgon hunts by tracking blood, similar

00:08:05.539 --> 00:08:06.539
to a shark.

00:08:06.539 --> 00:08:09.890
When it catches up with him, The Demogorgon
is able to warp Will into the Upside-Down

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:14.800
by weakening the fabric between the dimensions,
and like a shark, the creature closes in on

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.800
it’s meal.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.800
(impact)

