00:09:16.098 --> 00:09:20.000
(mysterious music)

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:24.141
After chasing the Demogorgon off by firing
the gun, Will wanders around the Upside-Down’s

00:09:24.141 --> 00:09:27.750
version of his house where he struggles to
communicate with his mom, or anyone from the

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:31.690
top side. Will explores the distorted version
of his house, and eventually falls asleep

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.260
beneath the Jaws poster in his mock-room,
maybe a clue about the creature’s blood

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.410
sensing abilities.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.640
Back on the surface, the town itself is temporarily
thrown into a seemingly lack-luster disarray

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.180
when it’s announced that Will Byers went
missing on his way home. Even Police Chief

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:48.390
Hopper initially takes the information almost
light-heartedly when Joyce includes the detail

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:52.140
that Will is a target of bullying at school,
along with Will’s father calling him

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.000
- ...a queer. Said he was a f*g.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.930
- This line of questioning, along with Joyce
begging Hopper to believe her, can parallel

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:01.790
a representation of Truman’s Loyalty Policies.
These insist that people should trust the

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:05.560
government to do what was necessary to keep
communism out of their neighborhoods. It’s

00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:09.460
only after Joyce answers Hopper’s questions
that he appears more interested in the case.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:13.220
Unfortunately for Hawkins, the monster that
infiltrated their town is far more than a

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:17.550
communist. The Demogorgon’s presence shows
the nature of the hysteria involved with speculating

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.110
that there is a communist hiding next door.
We can get a grasp on this representation

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:24.910
by using aspects from the first chapter of
Jeffery Cohen’s Monster Theory, along with

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:29.230
a historical perspective. The book presents
seven theses, each involving various creatures

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:33.340
being a symbolic representation of the cultures
that created them. For the infiltration of

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:37.230
Hawkins, we can refer to thesis number four,
where monsters are embodiments of what’s

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:40.620
different. Cohen writes that the creature
can be a form of “the Other” and in this

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.440
case, that “Other” is the Russians.

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:46.080
When Will wakes up to find himself still trapped
in the Upside-down, he tries to communicate

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:50.590
with his mom. The activity ends up attracting
the Demogorgon back to him as a form of connection

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.420
is established through his Supercomm. Luckily,
Will manages to scare the Demogorgon off a

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:57.950
second time by shooting at it but uses the
last of the ammunition.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:01.310
Meanwhile, search parties continue combing
the woods for Will, but his friends are not

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:05.810
content with sitting at home doing nothing.
Eleven tries to explain where Will is by flipping

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:08.860
their D&amp;D board over and placing Will’s
Wizard token in the center.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:09.860
- Hiding.

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.360
- From the bad man?

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.820
- [Gordon] There’s no such thing as the bad man.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:18.060
- Shut up Gordon, you don’t show up till Season
3. El places the Demogorgon token next to

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:21.560
Will’s Wizard piece. This explains how they
come to associate the name Demogorgon with

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:24.950
the monster, a name that sticks from then
on. I’ve also seen it suggested that the

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:29.640
Demogorgon token having two heads could be
a potential clue about duality if, in fact,

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.810
The Demogorgon is the Upside-Down version
of Eleven.

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:35.610
On Tuesday night, Nancy Wheeler brings her
friend Barb to a party at Steve Harrington’s

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:39.460
house. Barb ends up sitting by the pool after
cutting her hand and a blood drop falls into

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:43.560
the water, which is likely what drew the Demogorgon
to her. It appears behind her, as seen in

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:46.610
Jonathan Byers’s photographs, and brings
her into the Upside-Down.

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:49.930
Barb’s screams echo through the Upside-Down
as she’s dragged down into the empty pool

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:53.890
by the Demogorgon. Will, who is still in hiding
there can hear her screams, along with the

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:57.610
Demogorgon’s cry, and he runs out towards
the screams in an attempt to help her.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:01.130
But -- he’s too late, Will returns to the
Upside-Down version of his home and is able

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.960
to talk to his mom again, but also draws the
Demogorgon’s attention again. This time,

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:08.870
it goes for Mrs. Byers by ripping a hole in
the wall Andy Bernard style. It seems to be

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.440
able to sense where the veil between the worlds
is thinner, and it will prioritize getting

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.080
more people rather than always taking care
of the easiest target. I mean, it’s obviously

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:20.040
to make the show more dramatic… but if I
had to give it a logical reason… uh yeah,

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.260
let’s go with that thing I said. We see
a similar scene later on, this time Will takes

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:25.920
his Mom’s advice and runs for it.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:29.800
Then, in the underground lab, a scientist
explores the Upside-Down, communicating via

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:33.800
the microphone in his suit. He is basically
the Demogorgon equivalent of that light up

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:37.390
sign at Krispy Kreme that says hot donuts.
When the other scientists desperately try

00:12:37.390 --> 00:12:41.330
to pull him back, they end up with just some
spine and ribcage tied to the chain that was

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:44.250
around his waist. Hey, at least the food’s
not going to waste.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:47.960
Since the Demogorgon has infiltrated Hawkins
from the Upside-Down, it’s easy to say that

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:51.740
the Upside-Down itself is the equivalent of
the Iron Curtain. The Iron Curtain was an

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:55.900
implied wall in Europe that separated areas
controlled by the Soviet Union from Western

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.020
Allies.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:13:00.200
Those who crossed over to the Soviet side
of the curtain in the mid-80s may be greeted

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:04.220
with floating particles of ash similar to
those seen in the Upside-Down, because that’s

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.290
exactly what happened after the Chernobyl
disaster in 1986, when a reactor melted

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:12.270
down and forced evacuations for hundreds of
miles around the city of Pripyat.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.870
This could also explain why the Upside-Down
is mostly deserted, other than this strange

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.870
mutated creature. These attributes could also
be related to a meltdown in Three Mile Island

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:23.830
in Pennsylvania in the US, which was designed
to compete with the Russain advances in nuclear

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:24.830
technology.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.930
Just as Godzilla rose from Japan in the fallout
of their nuclear disaster -- history itself

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:33.110
can become the monster, and events of days
past can turn fears of contamination into

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:37.000
the horrors on your TV screen, or whatever
the **** you watch this show on.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.190
Nancy and Jonathan decide to hunt down the
Demogorgon in the woods. They stumble across

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:43.090
a dying deer, but before putting it out of
its misery…

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:48.270
...it’s abruptly yeeted back into the bushes.
Nancy ends up following the red trail through

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:52.520
a portal at the base of a tree and discovers
the Demogorgon… well, we’ve all seen someone

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:56.660
do this at the local discount buffet right?
It uses its squid-like face to rip its meal

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.030
to pieces, not even realizing that there are
other patrons, at the buffet.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:03.870
However, when the Demogorgon does realize
Nancy is there, it chases her into hiding

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:07.490
and traps her by blocking the portal back
to the real world, which tells us that the

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.950
monster does have some intelligence. Nancy
hears Jonathan’s voice calling from the

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.670
other side of the tree portal, which seems
to be closing, but Nancy isn’t the only

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:18.600
one who hears him. Will is also close enough
to hear his brother and ends up finding Nancy,

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.570
along with the portal, and the Demogorgon.

00:14:20.570 --> 00:14:24.290
Instead of going for the portal himself, Will
distracts the Demogorgon with a rock so Nancy

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.440
can escape. The Demogorgon takes the next
easy meal; the hunter, Henry, who had also

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:31.481
recently been trapped in the Upside-Down.
Exhausted and beginning to hallucinate, Will

00:14:31.481 --> 00:14:35.870
goes to the last safe place he can think of:
Castle Byers. Unfortunately for him, it’s

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.032
not as safe as he believes.

00:14:38.032 --> 00:14:41.642
(impact)

00:14:43.202 --> 00:14:47.210
(synth music)

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:51.410
As Will lays in his fort, Castle Byers, Eleven
visits him psycho-kinetically to tell him

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:55.381
that his mother is coming for him and to hold
on a little while longer. After she vanishes, Will

00:14:55.381 --> 00:14:59.700
starts muttering the lyrics to his favorite
The Clash song (OK Will, I see you) but unfortunately,

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.380
so does the Demogorgon, sending it straight
to his location.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.610
If Eleven and the Demogorgon are linked, it
stands to reason that when Eleven found Will,

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:10.450
she accidentally tipped off his location.
Basically anything she knows, the Demogorgon

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:14.440
knows, and this happens multiple times. We
see a similar concept with Will and the Mindflayer

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:15.550
in Season 2.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:19.100
It seems to be implied that Will is unable
to escape this time, but our friend flowerface

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:23.390
has bigger plans for him than simply making
him a midnight snack. Will finds himself deep

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:27.690
within the creature’s nest, with some kind
of facehugging organism plastered to his mouth.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.900
I’m guessing this is because Will is so
small that the Demogorgon would prefer to

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.640
make him a carrier rather than a meal. The
slug implanted within him appears to be the

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:35.640
Demogorgon’s offspring.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:39.540
I don’t know if that makes the Demogorgon
the male or the female, and I don’t really

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.840
want to think about it, so let’s just skip
to Nancy and Jonathan setting up the trap

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:46.470
on Friday, the 11th. They end up cutting their
own palms to lure it back to them with the

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:47.470
smell of their blood.

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.450
However, the monster is too powerful, and
knocks Jonathan down while surviving every

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.640
bullet Nancy has in her gun… which kind
of begs the question why it was afraid of

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:59.230
Will’s gun earlier on, but maybe it was
just a case of the creature not knowing its

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:03.070
own power -- like how if you tie down an elephant
with a small rope, it won’t realize it can

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.070
escape.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:07.381
Just before it’s about to strike Nancy,
Steve Harrington rushes in, and using the

00:16:07.381 --> 00:16:11.210
nailed bat and starts taking it to the monster
Kris Bryant style. The three of them manage

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:15.110
to get the monster’s foot stuck in the bear
trap and light it on fire. As Jonathan puts

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:19.360
the flames out, they find the beast gone with
only the dissolving remnants of flesh clinging

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:22.940
to the trap, presumably having been driven
back to its own dimension.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:26.510
While Chief Hopper and Will’s mom are rescuing
him from the Upside-Down, Dr. Brenner and

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:30.280
his people storm the school to try to kidnap
Eleven. She uses her abilities to squeeze

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:33.830
the brains of all the “Bad Men” threatening
her friends, but the use of her powers once

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:37.821
again causes a nose bleed and attracts the
Demogorgon. The kids run to try and get to

00:16:37.821 --> 00:16:39.390
safety in the science classroom.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:43.100
The boys scream for Lucas to get the wrist
rocket out as the Demogorgon breaks down the

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:47.110
door, following the scent of Eleven’s blood.
While the rocks don’t actually do much damage,

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:51.580
Eleven recovers just enough to send the monster
flying back into the wall and, with a parting

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:55.570
farewell, proceeds to disintegrate the Demogorgon,
disappearing into the Upside-down herself

00:16:55.570 --> 00:16:56.570
as she does so.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.930
It’s very interesting how when they come
face to face, they are practically mirror

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:03.720
images of each other, and the only way for
El to defeat it, or get rid of it, also hurts

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:08.199
her and transports her to the upside down.
This isn’t proof that she’s the Demogorgon

00:17:08.199 --> 00:17:12.949
and the Demogorgon is her, but I can’t ignore
the fact that she sees herself as the monster.

00:17:13.892 --> 00:17:15.175
- El!

00:17:15.175 --> 00:17:18.819
- [Eleven] Mike. I’m sorry.

00:17:18.819 --> 00:17:21.123
- Sorry? What are you sorry for?

00:17:21.123 --> 00:17:27.480
- The gate. I opened it. I’m the monster.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.630
- So if El is the Demogorgon, and she survives
this battle, seemingly being transported back

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:35.720
into the Upside-Down it’s possible that
old flowerface survives too, just as the idea

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:39.419
of communism has somehow survived many wars
over many years.

00:17:39.419 --> 00:17:42.600
Or, it could just be that the creature seen
in Russia at the end of the third season is

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:46.129
just another member of the same species. Either
way, the analogy probably stands.

00:17:46.129 --> 00:17:50.309
If you want to see the histories of more horror
monsters, click that playlist on the left.

00:17:50.309 --> 00:17:54.159
We’ve got more Stranger Things episodes
coming, so remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:17:54.159 --> 00:17:58.480
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell
for notifications and I’ll see you in the

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.890
next one. Assuming we both survive.

